RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
May 12, 2008
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in regular session on this date
beginning at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR-Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL
MEMBERS-Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne,
Mr. Segrave and Mr. Valdez.
Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Claudia Angelos,
City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of (CA) are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests, in which event the item
will be removed from the Consent Agenda and considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.
(CA)
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON APRIL 28,
2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
(CA)
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON MAY 5,
2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Valdez.
Upon inquiry, Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, reviewed information available for a voucher payable to
Teton Group and Alberta Anderson ($40,000), purchase of storm water easement for Masonway
Roadway Improvement Project.  Upon inquiry regarding a voucher payable to Ziebart Consulting,
LLC ($6,405.46), consultant fees, brief discussion was held on reports received from Mr. Ziebart.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body with the exception of Mr.
Laybourn voting “no”.
