for animals running at large.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” - all members of the governing
body.  Discussion continued on mandatory altering and microchipping and animal owner
responsibility, when cited with a 2 offense, to provide proof to Cheyenne Animal Control that the
nd
animal had been altered and microchipped.  Upon inquiry, Police Chief Bob Fecht, Cheyenne Animal
Shelter/Control board member, explained procedures that would be followed if an animal owner did
not comply with altering and microchipping requirements.  Further discussion followed regarding
enforcement issues; Animal Control officers’ employment package and retaining quality officers; non-
City employees enforcing City code animal laws, and mandatory court appearances for animal owners
who violate certain ordinance provisions.  Upon inquiry, City Attorney Claudia Angelos expressed
her opinion that ordinance provisions involving microchipping would not apply to turtles, but would
apply to animals with vertebraes.  Main motion as amended carried.  Voting “yes” - all members of
the governing body with the exception of Ms. Case voting “no”.  (#3801)
