Motion (per consent agenda) carried. (#5242)
Proposal for professional services between the City of Cheyenne, Parks and Recreation
Department, and S&S Builders LLC, for design of a pre-engineered steel building to be used as a
maintenance building, at the Dutcher Field Baseball Complex (SLIB grant and general fund).  Mr.
Segrave moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $56,955.00, seconded by Mr. Pierson.
Discussion followed on the design/build process as allowed by a change in state statutes and this
being the first City project to utilize the process; difference in bidding procedures from traditional
design/bid/build process, and design elements contained in Plan Cheyenne relative to the building.
Upon inquiry, Tim Grote, Parks Project Manager, advised the design process will include any
elements required by the City and explained the structure rendering that had previously been
submitted was a preliminary, not a final, design.  Discussion continued on contractor-subcontractor
relationship; comments in support and non-support of trying the design/build process, use of local
contractors, and PlanCheyenne elements.  Mr. Grote advised the site plan is currently under review
for the project and staff comments that are submitted, including building elements, will be addressed.
He reported an RFP (request for proposals) was issued and discussed  the design/build concept and
proposed costs affiliated with design vs. construction phases.  Comments continued on the
design/build concept, fiscal accountability, inclusion of building design elements, accelerated schedule
and anticipated cost savings by utilizing the new process, and lack of information on design/build
procedures.  Upon inquiry, Mr. Grote explained anticipated cost savings by using a design/build
process to coordinate design and construction areas, and Rudy Apodaca, Purchasing Director,
provided information on the design build team, which would include an architect retained by the
contractor.  Mr. Grote clarified he would be serving as the City project manager; provided
information on the guaranteed maximum price that will be submitted by the contractor through the
design process, and stated staff has determined for this first project under the design/build process,
if the item were approved, a second agenda item would be submitted for governing body review
relative to the contractor’s guaranteed maximum price to construct the building and affiliated design
elements.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” - all members of the governing body with the exception of
Ms. Case and Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.  (#5243)
